    <bpmn:process id="W_W5489" name="W5489. Typhoon &amp; Calamity Demand-Surge Forecasting and Pre-Positioning" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: PAGASA tropical-cyclone advisory (low-pressure area → Signal); pre-season (April–May) calamity-readiness cycle
Frequency: Continuous monitoring (Jun–Nov peak) + pre-season build + per-storm response
Volume: ~20 named storms/yr entering PAR; flood-control SKU surge of 3–10× baseline across the affected region&#x27;s ~20–60 stores
Owner: S&amp;OP/IBP Lead (Supply Chain &amp; Logistics)
Participants: Demand Planning, Supply Planning, DC Operations (links to VS-04), Logistics/Fleet (links to VS-06/VS-110), Sourcing (links to VS-122/VS-03), Merchandising (links to VS-01), Store Ops (links to VS-07/VS-177), Disaster Response/BCP (links to VS-69), Quality (links to VS-31)
Source: workflow W5489 — Typhoon &amp; Calamity Demand-Surge Forecasting and Pre-Positioning</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5489_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5489_Lane1" name="Demand Planning">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5489_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5489_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5489_Lane2" name="S&amp;OP">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5489_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5489_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5489_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5489_Start4" name="PAGASA tropical-cyclone advisory (low-pressure area → Signal); pre-season (April–May)…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5489_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5489_Task5" name="Demand Planning maintain a flood-control/calamity SKU cluster (sandbags…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Demand Planning maintain a flood-control/calamity SKU cluster (sandbags, plywood, lumber, nails/screws, tarps, water pumps, flashlights/batteries, PVC pipes, waterproofing, generators) and a per-region surge model calibrated on prior storms (Haiyan/Yolanda, Odette/Rai, Karding) — base demand × Signal-strength × region exposure — refreshed each pre-season
Responsible (R): Demand Planning
Accountable (A): S&amp;OP/IBP Lead
Duration: Pre-season + per storm</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5489_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5489_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5489_Task6" name="On PAGASA forecast track, S&amp;OP/IBP run the surge scenario for the likely…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: On PAGASA forecast track, S&amp;OP/IBP run the surge scenario for the likely landfall region: forecast SKU spike, days-of-supply gap vs on-hand + in-transit, and the pre-positioning plan (push build-forward from the nearest DC, expedite local sourcing links to VS-122/VS-03, inter-island transfer links to W5492) timed against the 45–90-day import lead where import SKUs are involved
Responsible (R): S&amp;OP/IBP / Supply Planning
Accountable (A): S&amp;OP/IBP Lead
Duration: 4–8 hrs per storm scenario</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5489_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5489_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5489_Task7" name="S&amp;OP/IBP/Supply execute pre-positioning (DC special-build, store…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: S&amp;OP/IBP/Supply execute pre-positioning (DC special-build, store forward-stocking of the calamity cluster, 3PL capacity pre-book links to VS-06/VS-110), set allocation/rationing rules for the event, interface the DTI price-freeze constraint (links to W5496), and run the post-storm sell-down/rebalancing to avoid stranded post-event stock
Responsible (R): S&amp;OP/IBP / DC Ops / Store Ops
Accountable (A): S&amp;OP/IBP Lead
Duration: Per storm + 1–2 wks sell-down</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5489_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5489_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5489_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5489_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-613 (ensure controlled execution — Calamity, Seasonality &amp; Philippine-Retail Demand–Supply Dynamics (PA-127.4).) | - operational: per-region surge model calibrated on prior storms and refreshed pre-season; operational: post-event rebalancing to prevent stranded stock; operational: RA 7581 price-freeze interface (W5496)
Owner: S&amp;OP/IBP Lead (Supply Chain &amp; Logistics)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W5489_Assoc10" sourceRef="W5489_Annotation9" targetRef="W5489_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
