    <bpmn:process id="W_W5490" name="W5490. Ber-Months (September–December) Seasonal Ramp Planning" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual seasonal cycle; MFP/OTB refresh (links to VS-101)
Frequency: Annual plan + monthly re-forecast Sep–Dec
Volume: The largest demand quarter: holiday décor/gift items, lighting, appliances, furniture + renovation surge ahead of the holidays + 13th-month-pay-driven discretionary spend across 200 stores
Owner: S&amp;OP/IBP Lead (Supply Chain &amp; Logistics)
Participants: Demand Planning, Merchandising (links to VS-01/VS-101), Supply Planning, Sourcing/Import (links to VS-122), Marketing (links to VS-14/VS-58), DC Operations (links to VS-04), Store Ops (links to VS-07), Finance/FP&amp;A (links to VS-17.4/VS-101)
Source: workflow W5490 — Ber-Months (September–December) Seasonal Ramp Planning</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5490_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5490_Lane1" name="Demand Planning">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5490_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5490_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5490_Lane2" name="S&amp;OP">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5490_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5490_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5490_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5490_Start4" name="Annual seasonal cycle; MFP/OTB refresh (links to VS-101)">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5490_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5490_Task5" name="Demand Planning build the ber-months demand profile per category/region from…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Demand Planning build the ber-months demand profile per category/region from prior-year actuals (Sep ramp → Oct/Nov peak → Dec Noche Buena/Christmas peak → Jan drop), segment holiday-gift vs renovation-surge vs 13th-month-discretionary components, and size the peak vs steady-state lift
Responsible (R): Demand Planning / Insights
Accountable (A): S&amp;OP/IBP Lead
Duration: Annual + monthly Sep–Dec</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5490_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5490_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5490_Task6" name="S&amp;OP/IBP translate the profile into a phased supply/import pre-build that…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: S&amp;OP/IBP translate the profile into a phased supply/import pre-build that respects the 45–90-day import lead (order by Jun–Jul for Sep landfall), align to the MFP/OTB and markdown budget (links to VS-101/W3922), and reserve DC throughput, store-labor peak (links to VS-19.3), and 3PL capacity (links to VS-06/VS-110) for the peak weeks
Responsible (R): S&amp;OP/IBP / Supply / Sourcing / Finance
Accountable (A): S&amp;OP/IBP Lead
Duration: Annual + monthly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5490_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5490_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5490_Task7" name="S&amp;OP/IBP run the in-season re-forecast (sell-through vs plan by week), trigger…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: S&amp;OP/IBP run the in-season re-forecast (sell-through vs plan by week), trigger markdown/rebalance on under/over-performance (links to VS-101/VS-64), and plan the post-holiday clearance and inventory burn-down to hit turn and avoid obsolete carry-over (links to W3908 phase-out)
Responsible (R): S&amp;OP/IBP / Merchandising / Supply
Accountable (A): S&amp;OP/IBP Lead
Duration: Weekly Sep–Jan</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5490_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5490_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5490_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5490_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-613 (ensure controlled execution — Calamity, Seasonality &amp; Philippine-Retail Demand–Supply Dynamics (PA-127.4).) | - operational: prior-year-actuals demand profile with component segmentation; operational: weekly in-season sell-through re-forecast and burn-down; operational: RCCP capacity reservation for peak weeks
Owner: S&amp;OP/IBP Lead (Supply Chain &amp; Logistics)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W5490_Assoc10" sourceRef="W5490_Annotation9" targetRef="W5490_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
