    <bpmn:process id="W_W5491" name="W5491. Summer Season (Aircon, Garden &amp; Dry-Season Construction) Planning" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual seasonal cycle (Mar–May peak); MFP refresh (links to VS-101)
Frequency: Annual plan + monthly re-forecast Mar–May
Volume: Summer peak: aircon/appliances, garden/outdoor, water tanks/pumps, plus the dry-season construction peak (the fastest building window in the PH calendar) driving lumber/cement/steel/tools
Owner: S&amp;OP/IBP Lead (Supply Chain &amp; Logistics)
Participants: Demand Planning, Merchandising (links to VS-01/VS-101), Supply Planning, Sourcing/Import (links to VS-122), DC Operations (links to VS-04), Store Ops (links to VS-07), Trade/B2B (links to VS-11/VS-107/W5493), Finance (links to VS-17.4)
Source: workflow W5491 — Summer Season (Aircon, Garden &amp; Dry-Season Construction) Planning</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5491_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5491_Lane1" name="Demand Planning">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5491_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5491_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5491_Lane2" name="S&amp;OP">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5491_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5491_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5491_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5491_Start4" name="Annual seasonal cycle (Mar–May peak); MFP refresh (links to VS-101)">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5491_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5491_Task5" name="Demand Planning build the summer demand profile: aircon/appliance heat-wave…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Demand Planning build the summer demand profile: aircon/appliance heat-wave elasticity, garden/outdoor seasonality, water-tank/pump demand, and the dry-season construction uplift on lumber/cement/steel/tools (trade/B2B links to VS-11/VS-107/W5493), segmented by region (summer hits different regions on different timing)
Responsible (R): Demand Planning / Insights / Trade
Accountable (A): S&amp;OP/IBP Lead
Duration: Annual + monthly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5491_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5491_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5491_Task6" name="S&amp;OP/IBP phase the supply/import pre-build (aircon/appliances are import-heavy…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: S&amp;OP/IBP phase the supply/import pre-build (aircon/appliances are import-heavy, 45–90-day lead → order by Dec–Jan), align to OTB (links to VS-101), and reserve install/service capacity (links to VS-12) and DC/3PL capacity for the aircon bulky-flow and the construction-material volume
Responsible (R): S&amp;OP/IBP / Supply / Sourcing
Accountable (A): S&amp;OP/IBP Lead
Duration: Annual + monthly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5491_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5491_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5491_Task7" name="S&amp;OP/IBP run in-season re-forecast driven by actual heat/temperature and…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: S&amp;OP/IBP run in-season re-forecast driven by actual heat/temperature and construction-permit activity signals (demand sensing links to W3910), trigger rebalance/expedite on heat-wave spikes, and manage the aircon installation backlog and the post-summer garden sell-down
Responsible (R): S&amp;OP/IBP / Supply / Store Ops
Accountable (A): S&amp;OP/IBP Lead
Duration: Weekly Mar–Jun</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5491_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5491_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5491_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5491_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-613 (ensure controlled execution — Calamity, Seasonality &amp; Philippine-Retail Demand–Supply Dynamics (PA-127.4).) | - operational: region-segmented summer profile incl. construction uplift; operational: demand-sensing-driven in-season re-forecast; operational: install-capacity reservation
Owner: S&amp;OP/IBP Lead (Supply Chain &amp; Logistics)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W5491_Assoc10" sourceRef="W5491_Annotation9" targetRef="W5491_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
