    <bpmn:process id="W_W5492" name="W5492. Inter-Island Inventory Rebalancing and Allocation Under Disruption" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Regional disruption (typhoon landfall, port closure/congestion, DC outage, demand spike) or structural imbalance surfaced in supply review (links to W3913)
Frequency: On disruption + monthly structural rebalance
Volume: 4-DC archipelago network (Mindanao/Visayas/South-Luzon/North-Luzon) serving 200 stores; inter-island transfers and rationed allocation during events
Owner: S&amp;OP/IBP Lead (Supply Chain &amp; Logistics)
Participants: Supply Planning, DC Operations (links to VS-04), Logistics/Inter-Island Freight (links to VS-06/VS-66/VS-110), Store Ops (links to VS-07/VS-177), Merchandising (links to VS-01), Finance/SCF (links to VS-105), Sourcing (links to VS-122/VS-03)
Source: workflow W5492 — Inter-Island Inventory Rebalancing and Allocation Under Disruption</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5492_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5492_Lane1" name="S&amp;OP">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5492_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5492_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5492_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5492_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5492_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5492_Start3" name="Regional disruption (typhoon landfall, port closure/congestion, DC outage, demand spike)…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5492_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5492_Task4" name="S&amp;OP/IBP/Supply detect the regional imbalance or disruption impact: affected…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: S&amp;OP/IBP/Supply detect the regional imbalance or disruption impact: affected DC/region, days-of-supply by SKU, port/RORO/batch availability (links to VS-06/VS-66), and quantify the gap vs demand, including the typhoon-surge case (links to W5489) and the import-port-congestion case (links to W3915)
Responsible (R): S&amp;OP/IBP / Supply / DC Ops
Accountable (A): S&amp;OP/IBP Lead
Duration: 4–8 hrs per event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5492_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5492_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5492_Task5" name="S&amp;OP/IBP decide the reallocation: inter-island transfer from surplus DCs (links…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: S&amp;OP/IBP decide the reallocation: inter-island transfer from surplus DCs (links to VS-04/VS-06/VS-66), rationed allocation to stores prioritized by A-item/service/contractual obligation (B2B links to W5493), substitute SKU mapping (links to W279/VS-01), and expedite/alternate-port sourcing where the disruption is prolonged
Responsible (R): S&amp;OP/IBP / Supply / Logistics
Accountable (A): S&amp;OP/IBP Lead
Duration: 4–8 hrs per event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5492_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5492_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5492_Task6" name="S&amp;OP/IBP execute and track the rebalancing (transfer orders, RORO/inter-island…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: S&amp;OP/IBP execute and track the rebalancing (transfer orders, RORO/inter-island dispatch, allocation holds), reconcile post-event, and feed the structural-imbalance pattern into network design (links to VS-136/W3923) and the next cycle&#x27;s safety-stock policy
Responsible (R): S&amp;OP/IBP / DC Ops / Store Ops
Accountable (A): S&amp;OP/IBP Lead
Duration: Per event + monthly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5492_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5492_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5492_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5492_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-613 (ensure controlled execution — Calamity, Seasonality &amp; Philippine-Retail Demand–Supply Dynamics (PA-127.4).) | - operational: explicit allocation priority rules (A-item/contractual/margin); operational: post-event reconciliation and structural-pattern feed to network design; operational: multi-carrier inter-island redundancy
Owner: S&amp;OP/IBP Lead (Supply Chain &amp; Logistics)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
