    <bpmn:process id="W_W5494" name="W5494. New-Store-Opening Demand Induction and Initial-Stock S&amp;OP" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: New-store pipeline (10–15 new stores/yr, profile §3.1); store-opening schedule (links to VS-37/VS-20)
Frequency: Per store opening + monthly pipeline roll-up
Volume: 10–15 new stores/yr; each opening = one-time initial-stock drop + grand-opening spike + 13-week ramp-to-steady-state
Owner: S&amp;OP/IBP Lead (Supply Chain &amp; Logistics)
Participants: Demand Planning, Store Ops/Openings (links to VS-07/VS-37), Real Estate/Network (links to VS-20), Merchandising/Allocation (links to VS-01/VS-55), Supply Planning, DC Operations (links to VS-04), Logistics (links to VS-06/VS-110), Marketing (links to VS-14)
Source: workflow W5494 — New-Store-Opening Demand Induction and Initial-Stock S&amp;OP</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5494_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5494_Lane1" name="Demand Planning">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5494_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5494_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5494_Lane2" name="S&amp;OP">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5494_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5494_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5494_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5494_Start4" name="New-store pipeline (10–15 new stores/yr, profile §3.1); store-opening schedule (links to…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5494_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5494_Task5" name="Demand Planning build the new-store demand induction: initial…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Demand Planning build the new-store demand induction: initial assortment/stocking by store size/region (links to VS-01/VS-55), the grand-opening-week spike model from comparable-store history, and the 13-week ramp-to-steady-state curve, segmented by new-vs-mature-store-region
Responsible (R): Demand Planning / Merchandising / Insights
Accountable (A): S&amp;OP/IBP Lead
Duration: Per opening</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5494_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5494_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5494_Task6" name="S&amp;OP/IBP/Supply schedule the initial-stock build and inbound (DC pick/pack +…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: S&amp;OP/IBP/Supply schedule the initial-stock build and inbound (DC pick/pack + inbound to the new store links to VS-04/VS-06) against the opening date, pre-build import SKUs against the 45–90-day lead (links to VS-122), and align the opening to the consensus plan so the induction does not starve existing stores
Responsible (R): S&amp;OP/IBP / Supply / DC Ops
Accountable (A): S&amp;OP/IBP Lead
Duration: Per opening</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5494_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5494_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5494_Task7" name="S&amp;OP/IBP track the ramp actual vs the induction curve weekly for the first 13…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: S&amp;OP/IBP track the ramp actual vs the induction curve weekly for the first 13 weeks, trigger rebalance/replenishment tuning on over/under-performance, and feed ramp-learning back into comparable-store models (links to W3911) and network demand for the next openings
Responsible (R): S&amp;OP/IBP / Store Ops / Demand Planning
Accountable (A): S&amp;OP/IBP Lead
Duration: Weekly × 13 wks/store</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5494_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5494_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5494_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5494_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-613 (ensure controlled execution — Calamity, Seasonality &amp; Philippine-Retail Demand–Supply Dynamics (PA-127.4).) | - operational: induction aligned to the consensus plan to avoid starving existing stores; operational: 13-week ramp tracking with rebalance; operational: ramp-learning fed back into comparable-store models
Owner: S&amp;OP/IBP Lead (Supply Chain &amp; Logistics)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
